		<section id="about" class="welcome section"><div class="container two-col"><div><p class="eyebrow">Welcome to our home</p><h2>A living culture, carried forward together.</h2></div><div class="intro-copy"><p>We are the 16 Clans Katutubong Blaan of Bagong Pag-asa Tribal Community, a community rooted in kinship, stewardship, and the enduring wisdom of our ancestors.</p><p>This platform is a shared space for our people and guests to learn about Blaan identity, celebrate our living traditions, and support the work of protecting our heritage for generations to come.</p><a class="text-link" href="#history">Read our history <span>↗</span></a></div></div></section>

		<section class="vision-mission"><div class="container vm-grid"><article><span class="number">01</span><h3>Vision</h3><p>“I looked, and there was a white horse. Its rider held a bow; a crown was given to him, and he went out as a conqueror in order to conquer.” <small>(Revelation 6:2)</small></p></article><article><span class="number">02</span><h3>Mission</h3><p>“Then I saw when the Lamb broke one of the seven seals… I looked, and behold, a white horse, and he who sat on it had a bow; and a crown was given to him, and he went out conquering and to conquer.” <small>(Revelation 6:1–2)</small></p></article><article><span class="number">03</span><h3>Goals</h3><p>To introduce the vision of the rider on a white horse: faithful and true, judging and waging war in righteousness, crowned with many crowns. <small>(Revelation 19:11–16)</small></p></article><article><span class="number">04</span><h3>Objectives</h3><p>The Council helps inform indigenous cultural communities and inter-kingdom, inter-tribe, and inter-clan groups about aged-care reforms, and provides advice to government on aged care and ageing well.</p></article></div></section>

		<section id="mindanao" class="section reference-info"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Kultura at pamayanan</p><h2>Ang Mindanao at ang Kulturang Mindanawan</h2></div><p>Pagkilala sa lupain, kultura, at kasaysayan ng mga katutubong pamayanan.</p></div><div class="reference-copy"><article><h3>Ano ang Mindanao o Kamindanawan?</h3><p>Ito ang ikalawang pinakamalaking pulo sa Pilipinas. Ang Mindanao rin ang tawag sa isa sa tatlong pangunahing pangkat ng mga pulo sa bansa, kasama ang mga nakapalibot na maliliit na pulo. Tahanan ito ng maraming pamayanan, wika, at kultura.</p></article><article><h3>Ano ang kultura?</h3><p>Ito ang kabuuan ng pananaw, kaugalian, paniniwala, tradisyon, selebrasyon, sining, at pamumuhay na minana sa mga naunang henerasyon at patuloy na isinasalin hanggang sa kasalukuyan.</p></article></div><div class="reference-gallery"><img src="photo/image2.jpg" alt="Tanawin ng pamayanang Blaan"><img src="photo/a1.jpg" alt="Mga kasapi ng pamayanan"><img src="photo/a2.jpg" alt="Kabataan sa pagtitipon"><img src="photo/b3.jpg" alt="Detalye ng hinabing tela"></div><article class="blaan-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Kilalanin ang mga Blaan</p><h3>Isang katutubong pamayanan ng Timog Mindanao</h3><p>Ang Blaan ay isa sa mga katutubong pangkat ng Southern Mindanao. May mga pamayanang To Lagad o highlanders sa kabundukan ng Davao del Sur, South Cotabato, at Sultan Kudarat, at To Baba o lowlanders sa mga baybayin ng Sarangani at General Santos City at iba pang bahagi ng rehiyon. Wikang Blaan ang kanilang wika.</p><p>May sariling estrukturang pampolitika ang mga pamayanan, na pinamumunuan ng mga fulung o tribal chieftain. Kabilang sa mayamang materyal at di-materyal na kultura ang sayaw na maral, kasuotang lbung at daféng para sa kababaihan at tabih at utub para sa kalalakihan, awit na malëm, kuwentong flalók, instrumentong faglung at falimák, at mga kagamitang pangangaso at pandigma.</p></article></div></section>

		<section id="culture" class="section culture-section"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Our living heritage</p><h2>Culture & Traditions</h2></div><p>Knowledge lives in the hands, voices, and everyday practices of our people.</p></div><div class="culture-carousel" aria-label="Culture and traditions stories"><div class="culture-grid" id="culture-carousel-track"><article class="culture-card large"><img src="photo/b2.jpg" alt="Community members sharing a meal outdoors"><div><span>Community</span><h3>Kinship is our first language</h3></div></article><article class="culture-card"><img src="photo/b3.jpg" alt="Colorful handwoven textile detail"><div><span>Craft</span><h3>Weaving stories into every thread</h3></div></article><article class="culture-card"><img src="photo/b4.jpg" alt="Green forest landscape and mountain valley"><div><span>Stewardship</span><h3>Land as memory and responsibility</h3></div></article></div><div class="carousel-controls"><button class="carousel-button" type="button" data-carousel-direction="prev" aria-label="Show previous culture story" aria-controls="culture-carousel-track">&#8249;</button><button class="carousel-button" type="button" data-carousel-direction="next" aria-label="Show next culture story" aria-controls="culture-carousel-track">&#8250;</button></div></div></div></section>

